644	// sandboxHasNeverRun reports whether a sandbox has yet to run for the first
645	// time, which is the one case where creating it also starts it (see ensure).
646	//
647	// Pending is the obvious case. Awaiting-source is the same thing interrupted:
648	// the sandbox was created, parked for its client's push, and has been waiting
649	// ever since. Resuming it is still its first start.
650	//
651	// It reads the existence axis, not the runtime one, and that is the point: a
652	// sandbox that has reached `ready` has been created once already, so a later
653	// ensure — a re-pin, a spec change, a rebuild after the container was lost —
654	// rebuilds without starting, whatever the runtime last reported.
655	func sandboxHasNeverRun(state string) bool {
656		return state == model.SandboxStatePending || state == model.SandboxStateAwaitingSource
657	}
